{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xhas67uym2agsemtyzb3wadmwojyhiltuuaah64bf3iyakvaox2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/src/long.c` (68 lines, the only translation unit) exports exactly three symbols: the 1 MiB global `int array[262144]`, `perform_expensive_operations()` (100 rounds of `x*3+7`, `x^(x>>3)`, `x-(x<<1)`, `x/2 + x%7` per element), and `long_exec(unsigned seed)` (`srand`/`rand` fill → 2000 passes → XOR → `printf(\"%d\\n\", …)`).\n\n## Phase A artifacts (all mechanically derived)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 3/3 C symbols present in the Rust `.so` with identical names, `nm` kinds, and `array` size `0x100000`. Nothing missing, nothing extra, no stubs; no C module was left untranslated.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — greps prove the C has *zero* error returns/asserts/range/null checks, so the table enumerates the 14 degenerate/boundary/hostile inputs this ABI can actually receive (seed `0`/`1`/`0x80000000`/`UINT_MAX`, negative seed via signed prototype, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` overflow elements, fresh `.bss`, repeated calls, **extra FFI arguments** — legal because `void perform_expensive_operations()` has an unspecified parameter list, plus explicit \"no pointer params / no enum params\" rows).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 20 rows over the axes the C actually branches on (entry point × value shape × written subset × pass count × seed × observation channel × build profile × feature combo).\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` table** → one combination. `cargo check --no-default-features --all-targets` and `--all-features` both clean. The real build axis (dev vs. release: `opt-level=3`, `panic=\"abort\"`, `codegen-units=1`) is therefore treated as the equivalent axis and **every phase was run against both profiles**.\n\n## Results (both `.so`s loaded with `libloading`, never calling Rust directly)\n\n| suite | debug | release |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/phase_b_configs.rs` (C1–C19) | 18 passed (175 s) | 18 passed (99 s) |\n| `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` (E1–E14) | 11 passed (36 s) | 11 passed (20 s) |\n| `tests/symbols.rs` | 5 passed | 5 passed |\n\nFull 1 MiB array compared byte-for-byte on every row; random rows use fixed-seed SplitMix64 (64/32/16/8 trials).\n\n**Real end-to-end `long_exec`** (2000 iterations ≈ 5.2·10¹⁰ steps, ~520 s C + ~480 s Rust per seed, run as separate `#[ignore]` tests): seeds 42, 0, 7, `0xFFFFFFFF` all produced byte-identical captured stdout and XOR — and for seed 7 a byte-identical 1 MiB final `array`.\n\n## One real bug found and fixed\n\n`array` was only **4-byte aligned** in Rust, while gcc gives the 1 MiB C `.bss` array **32-byte** alignment (observable by any consumer of the exported data symbol). Fixed with `#[repr(C, align(32))] pub struct Array(pub [c_int; 256*1024])`; now asserted by `array_object_alignment_matches`. All e2e runs were redone after the fix.\n\nThe arithmetic core needed no changes; as controls, the C compiled at `-O0` and `-O2` and an independent Python two's-complement model both agree with the Rust bit-for-bit. `scripts/run_all.sh [e2e]` reproduces everything; `VERIFICATION.md` records the transcripts and the completion gate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":700,"cache_read_input_tokens":170545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":700,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32f9e73c-2ba1-4739-bf00-81f9996af83e","uuid":"1422a25e-f52b-4fe0-b50d-2ee8af1e2490","timestamp":"2026-08-18T00:26:36.786Z"}
